  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Determine the dimension of $\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}.$",
  "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns (or alternatively, $4$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $4.$",
